\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 What NCP-ArchPreview's concept module actually is\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Input:
\f1\b0  mean-pooled chunks of k = 4 tokens, continuous. Codes are never the input.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Module:
\f1\b0  a causal transformer over those chunks (8 layers at 8.9B, 4 layers in the 1B ablation). No recurrence.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Vocabulary:
\f1\b0  32 segments \'d7 128 codes \'d7 128 dimensions. The codebook learns only from the VQ loss, 
\f4 \uc0\u8214 
\f1 sg(c) \uc0\u8722  e
\f4 \uc0\u8214 
\f1 \'b2, where sg is stop-gradient.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Prediction:
\f1\b0  each segment's head gives a softmax \uc0\u960  over its codes. The prediction is \u265  = \u931 \u960 e, the \u960 -weighted average of the codes, and NCP = MSE(\u265 , sg(c_next)).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Injection:
\f1\b0  \uc0\u265  is added to the decoder's hidden state, shifted by one chunk. The decoder also gets the core's states through its CRC.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
What it's worth:
\f1\b0  the module alone gave about \uc0\u8722 0.007 loss; with the residual connections about \u8722 0.018; with the NCP loss \u8722 0.027 to \u8722 0.035.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Not in the paper:
\f1\b0  the head's form, the loss weights \uc0\u945  and \u946 , and any handling of dead codes.\
