\f3\b \cf0 In-weight two-hop
\f1\b0  (DiscoLoop's own task, about 700 epochs): every arm memorised its training data, and none generalised. ID test was 18\'9627%, OOD \uc0\u8804  1.5%; the 6-layer untied stack was best on ID (27%).\

\f3\b The key DiscoLoop finding:
\f1\b0  without the channel, the pass-1 state decodes the bridge 37\'9664% of the time. With the channel, the model stops putting the bridge there. It confidently decodes 
\f9\i other
\f1\i0  codes 93\'9698% of the time, so the channel became a private message rather than a clean bridge. I'm now testing whether that's caused by our quantised codebook (exact-vocabulary head) or by the fixed \uc0\u945  (DiscoLoop's learned gate). The untied and NCP-stack arms for the in-context task are still running.All runs are finished. I'll save the combined results and the test code, then write the review.# Concept module v1: review and test results\

