\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 Step 2: Deriving the design\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 From P1: no prelude or coda layers.
\f1\b0  Every attention layer in the module sits inside the loop, so any extra depth has to come from another pass. The readout is just a norm and the NCP head, which does no lookup.\

\f3\b From P1 and P2: one shallow layer per pass.
\f1\b0  One attention layer can do about one lookup (the QKV conv makes that one induction step). If a single pass could solve the task, the loop would go idle again. With one layer per pass, pass r can only add hop r. The loop becomes a step operator T, and R passes compute T
\f4 \uc0\u7487 
\f1 .\

\f3\b From P4: two streams, the input re-read every pass.
\f1\b0  This uses the same gated-residual grammar as the encoder:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls64\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
X
\f1\b0  = \uc0\u265 , the input concepts. Read every pass, never written.\
\ls64\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
S
\f1\b0  = the state, a scratchpad per concept position. It starts at S
\f6 \uc0\u8304 
\f1  = 0.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Every pass then sees the same kind of input: "the question (X), plus what I've found so far (S)". So the operator that works at pass 2 also works at pass 7. This is the TRM, Huginn and diffusion-paper recipe, and it replaces DiscoLoop's fix for the same mismatch.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 From P3: nothing unsupervised is given a meaning.
\f1\b0  No DiscoLoop channel, and no deep supervision on intermediate passes.\

\f3\b The equations.
\f1\b0  For each concept position m, with S
\f4 \uc0\u7504 
\f6 \uc0\u8317 \u8304 \u8318 
\f1  = 0, for passes r = 1, \'85, R:\
$$x=\\tfrac12\\big[g_X\\odot\\mathrm\{zcRMS\}(X)+g_S\\odot\\mathrm\{zcRMS\}(S)\\big],\\qquad S\\leftarrow S+s_a\\cdot\\mathrm\{Attn\}(x)$$\
$$x=\\tfrac12\\big[g_X\\odot\\mathrm\{zcRMS\}(X)+g_S\\odot\\mathrm\{zcRMS\}(S)\\big],\\qquad S\\leftarrow S+s_f\\cdot\\mathrm\{FFN\}(x)$$\
$$u_m=\\mathrm\{zcRMS\}\\big(S_m^\{(R)\}\\big)\\ \\to\\ \\text\{NCP head\}\\ \\to\\ \\pi,\\ \\hat c_\{m+1\};\\qquad \\text\{plan\}=(u,\\hat c)\\ \\text\{at\}\\ j^*(t)$$\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls65\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
g_X and g_S
\f1\b0  are the per-channel read gates, which learn how much to read from the question and from the scratchpad.\
\ls65\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
s_a and s_f
\f1\b0  are the write gates for the attention and FFN updates.\
\ls65\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Attn
\f1\b0  is the encoder's FULL layer at concept rate: causal over concepts, NoPE with a temperature, QKV conv, gated.\
\ls65\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The second x
\f1\b0  is re-read with the updated S before the FFN.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 Training and inference:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls66\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Training:
\f1\b0  sample R ~ U\{1, \'85, 4\} per step, with full backpropagation. The NCP loss comes after the last pass, and NTP reaches the module through the plan.\
\ls66\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Inference:
\f1\b0  R = 4 by default. Up to 8 passes can be spent on hard inputs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 graph TD\
  C["\uc0\u265 _1..\u265 _m (encoder)"] --> X["X: input stream, read every pass"]\
  Z["S\uc0\u8304  = 0"] --> L["ONE shared layer: read \{X, S\} 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  gated FULL attn + FFN 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  write S"]\
  X --> L\
  L -->|"pass r+1 (train R ~ U\{1..4\}; test up to 8)"| L\
  L --> U["u = zcRMS(S)"]\
  U --> H["NCP head 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  \uc0\u265 _\{m+1\}"]\
  U --> D["decoder reads (u, \uc0\u265 ) at j*(t)"]\
  H --> D\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

