\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 Step 1: GradCuit steering in the concept stream (hypothesis 1)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Why it's logical.
\f1\b0  GradCuit needs two things, and our architecture gives both by construction:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls71\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A short, direct credit path.
\f1\b0  A token's log-probability must be differentiable with respect to the latent through attention. In our model the concept core is the only long-range route, so a latent in its input stream X reaches every later token: token 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  decoder 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  plan u_\{j*\} 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  core passes 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  X. And because v2 re-reads X on every pass, the latent is applied on every pass.\
\ls71\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Mid-network placement.
\f1\b0  GradCuit found 25\'9650% depth best, and the concept core 
\f9\i is
\f1\i0  the middle of our network.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Your compression point helps too: at 1/4 resolution, each latent position steers a whole chunk-plan, not a single token.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

