\f3\b \cf0 \strokec3 What held up.
\f1\b0  Every derivation I re-checked against the code is correct: the causal read index, the one-hop-per-layer argument, the temperature numbers, the loss derivation, which gradients reach what, and the cost figures (\uc0\u8776  3.2 M parameters and \u8776  12 MFLOP/token in training at M2 size).\

\f3\b The main problem: the scratchpad stays too small.
\f1\b0  The layer reads S only after normalising it (rms). How sensitive that read is depends on \uc0\u8730 d_c / 
\f4 \uc0\u8214 
\f1 S
\f4 \uc0\u8214 
\f1 , the square root of the width over the state's size. Starting from S
\f6 \uc0\u8304 
\f1  = 0, 
\f4 \uc0\u8214 
\f1 S
\f4 \uc0\u8214 
\f1  stayed below \uc0\u8730 d_c for 12 passes in the trained loop that actually uses its recurrence. Two things follow:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls87\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The first pass got 25\'9649\'d7 more gradient than pass 4.\
\ls87\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 By pass 12 each extra pass only turned S by 1\'964\'b0.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 My original stability argument (\'a76.3) had missed this. The flat-gradient evidence I quoted came from the end-to-end run, where the loop was idle, so it said nothing about this case.\

\f3\b The proposed fix (A1): start S from one learned vector s
\f8 \uc0\u8320 
\f3  of size about \uc0\u8730 d_c, the same at every position.
\f1\b0  Because s
\f6 \uc0\u8320 
\f1  is identical for every input, it carries no information, so the reason for not starting S at the input still holds. I tested it on the concept-level task with 2 seeds per arm, training on hops 1\'963 only:\

