\f3\b Other findings, all corrected in the doc:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls88\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Documents must start at a multiple of 4 tokens.
\f1\b0  Otherwise a chunk spanning two packed documents mixes them. The earlier tests only used a 4-aligned boundary.\
\ls88\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Clip the codebook's gradient separately.
\f1\b0  Global clipping lets the VQ loss weight \uc0\u946  shrink every other gradient, so \u946  is not irrelevant as I had claimed.\
\ls88\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Decoder at more passes.
\f1\b0  It is trained on plans from 1\'964 passes, and running 8+ is untested end to end. This is now an M2 gate item.\
\ls88\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The floored plan gate only works if the plan's size is comparable to the decoder's residual stream.
\f1\b0  This carries to the decoder phase: bring the plan in as its own normalised stream.\
\ls88\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
